1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:02,100
Previously on Childrens Hospital...

2
00:00:02,233 --> 00:00:05,400
We're going to have to evacuate the hospital for 14 weeks.

3
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:08,866
However, I got us all a job as a private contractor at an army base in Japan.

4
00:00:08,866 --> 00:00:11,533
But we're ambassadors, so no betting on the operations.

5
00:00:11,533 --> 00:00:15,366
Are you paying me to keep quiet while you throw this surgery because you bet money on it?

6
00:00:15,366 --> 00:00:16,233
Uh-huh.

7
00:00:16,233 --> 00:00:18,900
You doctors have been a real asset to the base.

8
00:00:18,900 --> 00:00:23,900
You got the pediatric clinic on its feet and provided a lot of laughs along the way.

9
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:25,333
It's what we do.

10
00:00:25,333 --> 00:00:26,300
Ha!

11
00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:27,700
And zingers like that.

12
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:29,233
That I'm going to miss the most.

13
00:00:29,233 --> 00:00:32,600
But now you all have to go back to Childrens Hospital.

14
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:34,533
So we're nice and back to Brazil.

15
00:00:34,533 --> 00:00:37,466
Which, as we all know, is where we were based before we took this job in Japan.

16
00:00:37,466 --> 00:00:41,200
Which is, as we also know, where we've been.

17
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:43,433
And where we are. This is Japan.

18
00:00:43,433 --> 00:00:45,466
Owen Maestro, you're under arrest.

19
00:00:45,466 --> 00:00:47,133
Hey, what's going on? Come on, man.

20
00:00:47,133 --> 00:00:48,366
Owen!

21
00:00:53,466 --> 00:00:55,266
Owen, you can't!

22
00:00:55,266 --> 00:00:59,333
You've been found guilty of colluding with a criminal surgery-fixing ring.

23
00:00:59,333 --> 00:01:03,800
I hereby sentence you to 5 years in a maximum security penitentiary.

24
00:01:12,166 --> 00:01:15,366
By order of the Elder Council of Machines,

25
00:01:15,366 --> 00:01:19,900
all females of childbearing age shall surrender to a birthing farm for one year.

26
00:01:21,133 --> 00:01:25,000
What a bleak dystopian future we've found ourselves in.

27
00:01:25,233 --> 00:01:27,533
Thanks, guys! Hit the lights!

28
00:01:27,533 --> 00:01:32,233
I could never have written my first spec sci-fi fiction novel without you guys!

29
00:01:32,233 --> 00:01:35,933
Hey, before you guys go, listen, as you all know, my boyfriend Owen gets out of prison today,

30
00:01:35,933 --> 00:01:38,400
and, you know, he's been locked up for five years, so

31
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:40,233
make him feel at home.

32
00:01:40,233 --> 00:01:41,833
Oh, don't worry, Cat.

33
00:01:41,833 --> 00:01:46,265
I have him scheduled for a very difficult heart surgery today, so...

34
00:01:46,265 --> 00:01:47,633
That'll help.

35
00:01:47,633 --> 00:01:50,066
He hasn't performed surgery in five years. I mean, how's that going to help?

36
00:01:50,066 --> 00:01:54,765
In ways I couldn't possibly describe without incriminating myself.

37
00:01:54,765 --> 00:01:57,800
Hey, Cat. Uh, you know what Val and I do when we feel out of place?

38
00:01:57,800 --> 00:01:58,666
No.

39
00:01:58,666 --> 00:02:00,700
We look at our award.

40
00:02:00,700 --> 00:02:02,300
Have you guys seen this thing?

41
00:02:02,300 --> 00:02:04,133
Fastest team tonsillectomy.

42
00:02:04,133 --> 00:02:06,666
I mean, I don't know what got into us that day.

43
00:02:06,666 --> 00:02:09,833
It's like time just slowed down.

44
00:02:10,365 --> 00:02:13,000
I know a little something about that.

45
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:14,266
Owen's back!

46
00:02:14,266 --> 00:02:18,633
Pack! Owen's back! Pack is back!

47
00:02:22,233 --> 00:02:24,200
Thanks for not ratting me out.

48
00:02:24,200 --> 00:02:26,066
I'll make it up to you somehow.

49
00:02:26,066 --> 00:02:28,400
Hey, where's my lady?

50
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:30,233
Cat, I've been back in town for almost a minute.

51
00:02:30,233 --> 00:02:33,833
Why aren't you riding this thing in a supply closet right now?

52
00:02:35,466 --> 00:02:37,600
Because I'm pregnant.

53
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:40,233
Mazel tov!

54
00:02:40,233 --> 00:02:42,300
Fat!

55
00:02:42,300 --> 00:02:44,300
Look at those knockers!

56
00:02:44,300 --> 00:02:48,000
I've been standing behind counters for seven months waiting for the perfect time to tell you guys.

57
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:52,666
Owen, aren't you going to say anything?

58
00:02:53,466 --> 00:02:55,600
I don't know what to say.

59
00:02:55,600 --> 00:02:59,333
How about "hello" to your unborn child, say?

60
00:02:59,333 --> 00:03:02,833
Cat, I haven't seen you in five years.

61
00:03:02,833 --> 00:03:06,066
What do you call the conjugal visit we had seven months ago?

62
00:03:06,066 --> 00:03:10,033
That never happened, so I call it fiction.

63
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:16,800
Ah, my old office.

64
00:03:16,800 --> 00:03:22,100
Aw! Aw! What is that smell?

65
00:03:22,100 --> 00:03:24,200
There he is! Welcome back!

66
00:03:24,200 --> 00:03:28,300
I'm so sorry, we had to rezone your office as a public fart room,

67
00:03:28,300 --> 00:03:31,100
but you've always got a place here at Childrens.

68
00:03:31,100 --> 00:03:35,266
Unless, of course, your performance drops 4%, in which time you're out on your ass.

69
00:03:35,266 --> 00:03:37,700
It's corporate policy.

70
00:03:37,700 --> 00:03:41,200
So, have a good time, read a magazine, fart a little if you got one in the chamber.

71
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:44,300
What a pleasure to see you back, huh?

72
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:46,266
4%.

73
00:03:52,566 --> 00:03:55,766
Penny for your thoughts, my love. Who ripped a blast in here?

74
00:03:55,766 --> 00:03:59,400
Smells like broken promises to me, Cat.

75
00:03:59,400 --> 00:04:02,666
No, it really smells like a bathroom.

76
00:04:02,666 --> 00:04:05,900
How could you cheat on me and claim that baby is mine?

77
00:04:05,900 --> 00:04:08,233
How could you not remember?

78
00:04:08,233 --> 00:04:11,533
We made love in a stand-alone trailer like two wild animals.

79
00:04:11,533 --> 00:04:15,166
I'll never forget what you said right after your love exploded inside of me:

80
00:04:15,166 --> 00:04:18,500
"That one had a baby in it!"

81
00:04:18,500 --> 00:04:20,533
Why can't I remember?

82
00:04:20,533 --> 00:04:21,500
Listen,

83
00:04:21,500 --> 00:04:24,200
are you okay to do that surgery? It's in 3 hours.

84
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:28,300
I don't know, Cat. I just...

85
00:04:28,300 --> 00:04:29,933
Don't.

86
00:04:29,933 --> 00:04:31,600
Excuse me.

87
00:04:34,700 --> 00:04:37,200
And excuse me again.

88
00:04:43,466 --> 00:04:48,233
Listen, Owen, I think I can finally make things right between us.

89
00:04:48,233 --> 00:04:49,766
Check your hand.

90
00:04:51,533 --> 00:04:53,832
Not interested.

91 --> 00:04:56,366
Get interested! Your big surgery's in two hours.

92
00:04:56,366 --> 00:04:59,332
If you don't take a dive...

93
00:05:03,800 --> 00:05:05,800
I can't handle this.

94
00:05:08,266 --> 00:05:11,600
Sound just like you did back in the joint. Crying over your lack of ability to handle stuff.

95
00:05:11,600 --> 00:05:15,166
Dr. Ron Pippen! What's my old cellmate doing here?

96
00:05:15,166 --> 00:05:19,266
Still can't believe I shared a cell with the only other doctor in lockup. What a coincidence.

97
00:05:19,266 --> 00:05:22,866
I don't believe in coincidences.

98
00:05:22,866 --> 00:05:26,066
Then what are you doing here, Pippen, if it's not a coincidence?

99
00:05:26,066 --> 00:05:30,233
Just a remarkable concurrence of circumstances without any apparent connection.

100
00:05:30,233 --> 00:05:32,066
See you around, pal.

101
00:05:37,466 --> 00:05:40,266
Hey, there you are.

102
00:05:40,266 --> 00:05:43,866
So glad you finally remember our conjugal visit.

103
00:05:43,866 --> 00:05:45,300
I do?

104
00:05:45,300 --> 00:05:46,800
Yes!

105
00:05:46,800 --> 00:05:49,066
You said so an hour ago. You even gave feedback

106
00:05:49,066 --> 00:05:51,533
on color swatches for the nursery.

107
00:05:51,533 --> 00:05:54,066
I think I'm losing my mind.

108
00:05:58,666 --> 00:06:00,766
Oh, sorry. All yours.

109
00:06:11,666 --> 00:06:13,766
Knock knock.

110
00:06:13,766 --> 00:06:15,000
Hey.

111
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:16,566
How you doing, buddy?

112
00:06:16,566 --> 00:06:17,800
Not good, man.

113
00:06:17,800 --> 00:06:18,700
Yeah?

114
00:06:18,700 --> 00:06:20,000
I work...

115
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:21,500
in a fart room.

116
00:06:21,500 --> 00:06:22,233
Yeah.

117
00:06:22,233 --> 00:06:25,000
I don't remember putting a baby inside Cat.

118
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:27,166
Sy's going to fire me if I blow this surgery,

119
00:06:27,166 --> 00:06:30,233
but if I don't, Chief's going to kill me with her finger.

120
00:06:30,233 --> 00:06:33,966
You know what I do when I'm feeling blue? I like to look at my award.

121
00:06:33,966 --> 00:06:35,366
It's like time sai-

122
00:06:35,366 --> 00:06:38,400
Yeah, I know. Time said something, you guys took out some tonsils really fast.

123
00:06:38,400 --> 00:06:40,266
It's inspiring, really.

124
00:06:40,266 --> 00:06:42,300
I'm glad you like it because Val and I

125
00:06:42,300 --> 00:06:44,366
would like to give it to you

126
00:06:44,366 --> 00:06:46,066
as inspiration.

127
00:06:46,066 --> 00:06:47,066
Okay.

128
00:06:47,066 --> 00:06:49,166
Okay, so...

129
00:06:49,166 --> 00:06:50,966
now I have this.

130
00:06:50,966 --> 00:06:52,666
You're welcome.

131
00:06:53,933 --> 00:06:57,200
Excuse me. Sorry, thought I was done farting,

132
00:06:57,200 --> 00:07:00,466
but apparently, farting isn't done with me.

133
00:07:00,466 --> 00:07:02,166
Come on, man.

134
00:07:02,166 --> 00:07:04,133
You're probably going to want to leave. It's going to get pretty real in here.

135
00:07:04,133 --> 00:07:05,966
Yeah, I don't need to be here for this.

136
00:07:05,966 --> 00:07:07,333
Good luck on the surgery.

137
00:07:07,333 --> 00:07:08,800
Thank you.

138
00:07:11,366 --> 00:07:13,766
I guess I kind of oversold that.

139
00:07:14,266 --> 00:07:17,466
You got this. You got this.

140
00:07:21,500 --> 00:07:22,866
Owen!

141
00:07:22,866 --> 00:07:26,066
That doctor I've never seen before is a dead ringer for you!

142
00:07:26,066 --> 00:07:27,533
Cat...

143
00:07:27,533 --> 00:07:28,866
I'm Owen.

144
00:07:28,866 --> 00:07:32,832
This is my former cellmate, Ron Pippen.

145
00:07:32,832 --> 00:07:36,400
Looks like he's been pretending to be me to have sex with you.

146
00:07:36,400 --> 00:07:38,400
How could you do this, Pippen?

147
00:07:38,400 --> 00:07:41,200
I just took advantage of our uncanny resemblance.

148
00:07:41,200 --> 00:07:43,000
Good luck in there, Owen.

149
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:44,233
Chief!

150
00:07:45,900 --> 00:07:47,733
Is Madame Tussaud here?

151
00:07:47,733 --> 00:07:49,700
It's so real!

152
00:07:49,700 --> 00:07:51,200
Look at this!

153
00:07:51,200 --> 00:07:53,166
Chief, I'm

154
00:07:53,166 --> 00:07:55,266
Owen.

155
00:07:55,266 --> 00:07:57,200
What did you want?

156
00:07:57,200 --> 00:07:59,332
I just had my fingers sharpened.

157
00:07:59,332 --> 00:08:02,500
If you don't throw this surgery...

158
00:08:02,500 --> 00:08:04,066
you're dead.

159
00:08:04,066 --> 00:08:08,833
Owen, if you don't ace this surgery, you're dead.

160
00:08:08,833 --> 00:08:10,233
Professionally speaking.

161
00:08:10,233 --> 00:08:11,766
Over here, Sy.

162
00:08:11,766 --> 00:08:14,200
What, you want me to say it again into this mirror?

163
00:08:14,200 --> 00:08:17,300
Okay, everybody, get out!

164
00:08:17,300 --> 00:08:20,332
I'm doing surgery.

165
00:08:20,332 --> 00:08:22,866
Nurse, scalpel.

166
00:08:25,933 --> 00:08:29,200
Remember 4%.

167
00:08:30,300 --> 00:08:33,832
If you don't take a dive... you're dead.

168
00:08:33,832 --> 00:08:37,332
If you don't ace this surgery, you're out on your ass.

169
00:08:37,332 --> 00:08:41,200
I just had my fingers sharpened.

170
00:08:41,200 --> 00:08:44,033
Okay, pacemaker is in place.

171
00:08:44,033 --> 00:08:47,833
All we have to do now is turn it on.

172
00:08:51,833 --> 00:08:54,333
Turn it on.

173
00:09:05,333 --> 00:09:07,133
We're losing him!

174
00:09:10,033 --> 00:09:12,666
Don't do it, Owen.

175
00:09:15,733 --> 00:09:19,233
Chief, I'm no longer afraid of you.

176
00:09:19,233 --> 00:09:23,300
Are you no longer afraid of me?

177
00:09:23,300 --> 00:09:25,333
Pippen, you're in on this, too?

178
00:09:25,333 --> 00:09:27,533
Sing for him.

179
00:09:30,233 --> 00:09:33,300
Sorry, Owen.

180
00:09:41,033 --> 00:09:43,000
Clear!

181
00:09:44,300 --> 00:09:47,133
Let's finish this story.

182
00:09:50,066 --> 00:09:54,066
The nightmare is finally over for both of us.

183
00:09:54,066 --> 00:09:59,333
We're the chief shared a jail cell with the ringleader of the crime you were busted for.

184
00:09:59,333 --> 00:10:02,300
Sorry to put you through all of that. I had no choice.

185
00:10:02,300 --> 00:10:05,266
He had me by the balls.

186
00:10:05,266 --> 00:10:08,233
Hey, look in your hand.

187
00:10:10,333 --> 00:10:14,266
Oh, I love lemons and strawberries and grapes.

188
00:10:14,266 --> 00:10:18,066
Hey, Owen, now that we know this isn't your baby,

189
00:10:18,066 --> 00:10:20,066
I mean, what do we do?

190
00:10:20,066 --> 00:10:24,200
I would say for the next 13 weeks,

191
00:10:24,200 --> 00:10:25,766
let's just try not to think about it.

192
00:10:25,766 --> 00:10:29,200
Attention staff, will all available doctors please report to the emergency room?

193
00:10:29,200 --> 00:10:31,066
That is all. That is all.

194
00:10:31,066 --> 00:10:33,665
Well, let's get back to work, huh? Yeah.

195
00:10:33,665 --> 00:10:37,700
Oh, it's so good to be back in the old United States of America.

196
00:10:37,700 --> 00:10:39,533
Yeah, we're in Brazil.
